# Plaintext credential dumps (never commit).
# scripts/aws/cred holds AWS ROOT account keys AND the production RDS password in
# cleartext prose — its own header says so. Nothing matched before this rule:
# `.env`/`*.env`/`backend/credentials/` do not cover a file named `cred`, so a
# single `git add .` would have committed live credentials. Anchored with a
# leading slash so it matches only at the repo root, not any nested `cred` file
# that some future package might legitimately ship.
scripts/aws/cred
# Belt and braces: same reason, in case the file is ever moved or renamed.
aws/cred
aws/*.cred
aws/credentials*

# SSH private keys (never commit).
# /key/ucs-backend.pem is the EC2 bastion key the RDS tunnel script uses. Nothing
# matched before this rule, so `git add .` staged it. Leading slash anchors it to
# the repo root — the matching public key (.pub) is deliberately NOT ignored, so
# it stays committable.
/key/*.pem
/key/*.ppk
/key/id_rsa*
/key/id_ecdsa*
/key/id_ed25519*

# Flutter / Android build outputs (never commit)
/build/
**/build/
**/android/build/
**/.gradle/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# Firebase / app secrets (never commit)
**/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Credentials & private keys (never commit)
# Blocked by GitHub push protection on 2026-10-10: key/aws.txt (AWS access key
# ID + secret) and scripts/aws/cred (AWS secret) were committed. Both files are
# gone from the working tree, but their blobs are still inside commit 27bf39e2
# in this branch's history, so a push of master stays rejected until that commit
# is rewritten. These rules only stop them being re-added.
*.pem
*.ppk
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
key/aws.txt
key/*.pem
scripts/aws/cred
scripts/aws/cred.*
aws.txt
aws-credentials.txt
credentials.txt
creds.txt

# Plaintext passwords committed under `others/imp files/aws/`. The directory is
# ignored below, but gitignore does NOT apply to a file that is already tracked --
# and this one is, because it arrived from origin/master. It has to be untracked
# (git rm --cached) as well as ignored, or every `git add -A` keeps shipping it.
others/imp files/aws/

/client/windows
/client/android
/apps/beneficiaries/Secugen Android
/apps/beneficiaries/Secugen Windows
/others/imp files

